    "title": "Knicks Dominate Nets with Record-Breaking Victory",
    "text": "• The New York Knicks defeated the Brooklyn Nets 120-66, ending a four-game losing streak.\n• The 54-point victory is the most lopsided win in Knicks franchise history.\n• Jalen Brunson scored 20 points.\n• Landry Shamet scored 18 points in 15 minutes, going 6-for-6 from 3-point range.\n• The Knicks shot 57.5% from the field and led by as much as 59 points.\n• The Knicks had lost nine of their previous 11 games.\n• The Knicks held a players-only meeting after a loss to the Dallas Mavericks.\n• The Knicks have won the last 13 meetings against the Nets.\n• The Knicks outscored the Nets 12-0 in second-chance points and 29-4 on the fast break.\n• The Knicks will play the Philadelphia 76ers next.",
